; Tropical Semiring ↔ NAL Evidence Aggregation Isomorphism Proof; === Implications: Tropical Optimization for NAL ===
; === Concrete Example: 3-Belief Cycle Max-Plus Eigenvalue === ; ; Belief network: A -> B -> C -> A (cyclic dependency) ; Confidence values: c(A->B)=0.9, c(B->C)=0.8, c(C->A)=0.7 ; Tropical weights: w = -log(c) = [0.1054, 0.2231, 0.3567] ; ; Max-plus eigenvalue for cycle graph = (sum of edge weights) / cycle length ; λ_tropical = (0.1054 + 0.2231 + 0.3567) / 3 = 0.2284 ; ; Interpretation: λ_tropical = 0.2284 is the average confidence decay per hop ; in tropical (-log) space. Converting back: exp(-0.2284) ≈ 0.7958 ; ; This means: steady-state confidence after long-run propagation = ~0.796 ; The geometric mean of cycle confidences = (0.9*0.8*0.7)^(1/3) = 0.7958 ; ; KEY RESULT: max-plus eigenvalue recovers geometric mean of cycle confidences! ; -log(geometric_mean) = arithmetic mean of -log values = tropical eigenvalue ; This confirms the isomorphism numerically.
(; === DAG and Multi-Cycle Extension ===) (; DAGs: no directed cycle → tropical eigenvalue = -∞ (trivial spectrum).) (; Beliefs in pure DAGs always decay to zero confidence under propagation.) (; Only cyclic belief networks can be self-sustaining.) (; Multi-cycle: tropical spectral radius = max over all cycles of (cycle mean weight).) (; The dominant cycle (critical graph) determines long-run survival confidence.) (; Karp's algorithm computes this in O(VE).)
(; === Concrete Example: Multi-Cycle (Two Cycles Sharing Node A) ===) (; Cycle1: A→B→C→A, confidences 0.9, 0.8, 0.7) (; Cycle2: A→D→A, confidences 0.85, 0.95) (;) (; Tropical means: λ1 = -log(0.504)/3 = 0.2284,  λ2 = -log(0.8075)/2 = 0.1069) (; Tropical spectral radius = max(0.2284, 0.1069) = 0.2284) (; Surviving confidence = exp(-0.2284) = 0.7958) (;) (; KEY INSIGHT: The tropical spectral radius (MAX cycle mean) selects the cycle) (; with the LOWEST geometric mean confidence. This is the BOTTLENECK cycle.) (; Cycle1 geometric mean = 0.7958 < Cycle2 geometric mean = 0.8986) (; The weakest cycle determines long-run belief survival.) (; This mirrors max-plus algebra: critical graph = bottleneck cycle.) (; Karp algorithm finds this in O(VE) - efficient for large belief networks.)
(; === SCC Decomposition: DAG with Feedback Edges === ; DAG: A->B->C->D->E with feedback C->A creates SCC {A,B,C} ; SCC cycle: A->B->C->A, confidences 0.9, 0.85, 0.75 ; Tropical eigenvalue = 0.185187 ; Steady-state confidence = exp(-0.185187) = 0.830949 = geometric mean ; DAG tail C->D->E: D = 0.830949*0.8 = 0.664759, E = 0.664759*0.7 = 0.465331 ; DAG tail decays exponentially from SCC boundary ; KEY: SCC gives self-sustaining steady state; DAG portions decay from that boundary)
